WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.482
Week 9: Daily Routine and Reflexive Verbs. sequence a routine say what is happening now compare schedules

2
00:00:07.482 --> 00:00:14.836
Cultural lens. Work-life rhythms, siesta stereotypes versus reality, and shared household labor.

3
00:00:14.836 --> 00:00:27.270
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:39.277
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:39.277 --> 00:00:48.490
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:48.490 --> 00:01:13.553
Model language. Me levanto a las seis y media. — I get up at six thirty. Después de vestirme, preparo el desayuno. — After getting dressed, I prepare breakfast. Ahora estoy esperando el tren. — I am waiting for the train now. Los niños se acuestan temprano. — The children go to bed early. ¿A qué hora te despiertas? — What time do you wake up?

7
00:01:13.553 --> 00:01:23.707
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
